sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant Route as OpenShift Route<br/>(trustyai)
    participant Svc as ClusterIP Service<br/>80/TCP
    participant TrustyAI as trustyai-service<br/>8080/TCP Quarkus
    participant PVC as PersistentVolumeClaim<br/>/inputs
    participant Prometheus as Prometheus
    participant KServe as KServe / ModelMesh
    participant K8sAPI as OpenShift API Server

    Note over TrustyAI: Init Phase
    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        TrustyAI->>K8sAPI: oc apply model-serving-config ConfigMap<br/>(init container: config-map-overrider)
        K8sAPI-->>TrustyAI: ConfigMap created
        Note over KServe: model-serving-config registers<br/>http://trustyai-service.$ns/consumer/kserve/v2<br/>as payload processor
    end

    Note over TrustyAI: Runtime Phase

    rect rgb(255, 248, 240)
        Note over Client,TrustyAI: External Access Flow
        Client->>Route: HTTP Request
        Route->>Svc: Forward (port 80)
        Svc->>TrustyAI: Forward (port 8080)
        TrustyAI-->>Svc: Response
        Svc-->>Route: Response
        Route-->>Client: HTTP Response
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over KServe,PVC: KServe Payload Ingestion Flow
        KServe->>TrustyAI: POST /consumer/kserve/v2<br/>Inference payloads
        TrustyAI->>PVC: Store inference data<br/>at /inputs
        TrustyAI-->>KServe: Acknowledgment
    end

    rect rgb(248, 240, 255)
        Note over Prometheus,TrustyAI: Monitoring Flow
        Prometheus->>TrustyAI: GET /q/metrics<br/>8080/TCP (scrape)
        TrustyAI-->>Prometheus: Metrics response<br/>(fairness & explainability metrics)
    end

    rect rgb(255, 255, 240)
        Note over TrustyAI: Health Probes
        Note right of TrustyAI: GET /q/health/live (liveness)<br/>GET /q/health/ready (readiness)<br/>Port 8080
    end
